meta {
  name: Me
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{probity_base_url}}/me
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{probity_api_key}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Describe the authenticated key and its company.

  Response: { key: { name, prefix, kind, scopes[] },
              company: { id, name },
              data_freshness: { last_synced_at } }

  data_freshness.last_synced_at is the most recent successful QBO/Plaid sync
  (null when neither has synced) — "Probity monitoring active, data current
  as of …".

  Good first request after setting `probity_api_key` — it confirms the key is valid
  and shows which scopes it carries. 401 on a missing/unknown/revoked/expired
  key.

  The key value starts with `probity_` (e.g. `probity_<prefix>_<secret>`).
  Keys minted before the 2026-10-05 rebrand used `foundry_<prefix>_<secret>`
  and still authenticate. Create keys in the app under Settings → API Keys;
  copy the one-time value into the `probity_api_key` secret.
}
